# Suppressions must name the control and the reason. An entry without a reason
# is a finding someone hid, and review should treat it as one. Everything not
# listed here fails the build.

# AVD-AWS-0104 — the data plane needs outbound internet for managed-service
# endpoints, package installation on the pipeline workers and object-store
# replication, and reaches it through the NAT gateway. Egress is already
# restricted by port; the destination cannot be narrowed further without pinning
# service addresses that AWS does not publish as stable ranges.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AVD-AWS-0132 — buckets are encrypted with SSE-KMS under the AWS-managed key.
# A customer-managed key is the stricter option, but it needs a key policy
# granting the service principals that write these objects, which has to be
# validated against a live account before it ships. Tracked, not dismissed: the
# data is encrypted, just not under our own key.
AVD-AWS-0132
